+- **No database access at all, for any player** (canonical or EA-only): everything is read from the in-memory read model RM1, the very row `getPlayer` uses, so no SQL was added to `readmodels/definitions.py`. A test makes `db.cursor` raise and still gets 200 for every sample player; the endpoint also keeps answering if the database disappears after startup (the 503 gate is the startup state). EA-only and canonical players get the same kind of answer: every player has an EA row, so `ea_ingame_value.availability` is `AVAILABLE` for all 16,107 (a whole-population test compares every response with the stored row).
+- **The EA in-game value is not a market value and not a model estimate**: the response contains no market value, model estimate, injury, identity or link; changing only the market-value table in a copy leaves this response unchanged and vice versa (tested). A NULL `value_eur_ingame` would be `NO_SOURCE_DATA` with a null amount, never 0 (the real data has none).
+- **`detailed_attributes` is PLANNED**: `availability = NOT_YET_INTEGRATED`, `attributes = null`, always, because `ea_fc26_attributes.raw_json` is NULL for every row (G1). Nothing (pace, finishing, ...) is invented or taken from another source.
+- Provenance: `ea_fc26`, its `dataset_version`, `fetched_at` (the EA field load time, whole seconds UTC) and `data_origin` `REAL_FULL`; identical in `provenance` and `ea_ingame_value.provenance`. `fetched_at` is NOT NULL in `player_field_values`, so the contract's nullable `fetched_at` never occurs in practice. `meta.contains_sample_data` is false.
+- `overall_rating` / `potential` are non-null in the contract although the columns are nullable: the existing startup invariant (`integrity_service`) refuses to serve ANYTHING if one is NULL, so the endpoint can never emit a null rating (tested on a corrupted copy: 503 everywhere).
+- Shared logic: the EA value / provenance construction was moved out of `build_summary` into `player_summary.ea_ingame_value` / `ea_provenance` (behaviour identical, covered by the existing tests) so that `getPlayer`, search and this endpoint can never diverge.
