 ## getPlayerInjuries behaviour decided in Step 4.5
 Same id grammar and errors as `getPlayer`. Still `SCHEMA_ONLY` in the contract: no injury source, no writer, no rows. EA-only (or a canonical player without a status row) -> `200 NOT_EVALUATED`, `checked_at` null, `records` []. Canonical -> the stored `injury_data_status` (today `NO_SOURCE_AVAILABLE` = "no source", never "no injuries"). `records` is read only when the stored status is `HAS_RECORDS` and is passed through as stored (no derived values; order `start_date`, `expected_return`, `id` ASC, NULLs last). No derived metric and no market-value impact. The contract itself is unchanged (0.4.0-draft); see gap G16 in `ARCHITECTURE_API.md` for what must be added to it before a real injury source exists.
 
+## getPlayerEaAttributes behaviour decided in Step 4.6
+Same id grammar and errors as `getPlayer`. Served entirely from the in-memory player index (no database access, no new SQL): `overall_rating`, `potential`, `preferred_foot`, the EA in-game value (NOT a market value; no market value or model estimate in the response) and provenance (`ea_fc26`, `REAL_FULL`). Every player has an EA row, so EA-only and canonical players are answered alike. `detailed_attributes` is PLANNED: `NOT_YET_INTEGRATED` / null until G1 stores the attributes. A NULL EA value would be `NO_SOURCE_DATA`, never 0. The contract itself is unchanged (0.4.0-draft); no ambiguity about PLANNED/null was found.
